; smf-running-status — the status byte that is not repeated.
;
; Three note-ons of one status, three note-offs of another, then a meta
; event that RESETS running status and two control changes after it. The
; writer's rule (consecutive channel messages of the same status share
; it; every meta and sysex resets) and the reader's are one rule read
; twice, which is what rung 1 asserts here.
(read)
(roundtrip)
